{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/301846-what-happens-when-a-wraith-resolves-a-fetter","id":301846,"title":"What happens when a Wraith resolves a Fetter?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-03T23:16:09-08:00","id":301846,"title":"What happens when a Wraith resolves a Fetter?","content":"I have read on the web that when a Wraith resolves a Fetter they become a Gaunt and they can travel more freely in the underworld. Could someone explain what that means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T00:26:39-08:00","id":301918,"title":"","content":"First off, you need to be aware of the rules that link Underworld travel and Fetter status (Wraith 2e, p.231): a wraith with unresolved Fetters, like most PCs, finds the tug of their Fetters more and more distracting the further they go from the Shadowlands. This is represented by an increase in difficulty to all rolls: in Stygia, it's +1, towards the Far Shores and the Labyrinth it's +2.<br /> <br /> Wraiths who have lost all their Fetters find they can only stay in the Shadowlands for very brief periods, lacking any anchors.<br /> <br /> It's rumoured that wraiths who resolve all their Fetters can travel anywhere in the Underworld at will, and that among them are the most powerful Stygian Gaunts and certain elder Heretics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:33:51-08:00","id":302608,"title":"","content":"How can fetters be resolved. Passions I get, but Fetters? How is loosing different from resolving ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:34:33-08:00","id":302696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/301846-what-happens-when-a-wraith-resolves-a-fetter?p=302608#post302608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can fetters be resolved. Passions I get, but Fetters? How is loosing different from resolving ?</div> </div> </div> </div>SHORT VERSION:<br /> Your Fetter is your baby sister whom you miss. You learn to accept the loss and let her go to live her own life instead of continuing to haunt her. Fetter resolved.<br /> <br /> As Passions are often connected to Fetters, resolving one tends to resolve the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T05:45:30-08:00","id":303215,"title":"","content":"So, if the little sister is killed, the Fetter is lost, which is bad for the wraith.<br /> If he decides or reaches an emotional state, in which he doesn't care for the sister that much any more, that is good.<br /> <br /> How about accepting that the sister was killed, would that turn &quot;lost&quot; into &quot;resolved&quot;?<br /> <br /> I always assumed that the &quot;rumour&quot; of resolving fetters were actually resolving passions... Although I thought it was akin to reaching Transcendence...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T06:11:46-08:00","id":303224,"title":"","content":"If the Fetter is destroyed, it results in a Harrowing. If the Wraith succeeds at the Harrowing, the Fetter is considered Resolved. If the Harrowing fails, it is considered lost. If they botch it, they may quickly find other Fetters being affected. As to resolving a Fetter after the fact, I don't recall ever seeing any rules on it. I would allow it my games though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T08:34:21-08:00","id":303321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/301846-what-happens-when-a-wraith-resolves-a-fetter?p=303215#post303215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if the little sister is killed, the Fetter is lost, which is bad for the wraith.<br /> If he decides or reaches an emotional state, in which he doesn't care for the sister that much any more, that is good.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more reaching an emotional state in which you can let something go. You still care about it, but you're no longer hung up on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always assumed that the &quot;rumour&quot; of resolving fetters were actually resolving passions... Although I thought it was akin to reaching Transcendence... </div> </div> </div>The relevant quote from Wraith 2e, p. 231: &quot;There are those rare wraiths who Resolved all of their Fetters, to whom rumor grants the ability to travel anywhere in the Underworld.&quot;<br /> <br /> I.E., their existence is a known thing, what they can do is a rumour.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T11:03:59-08:00","id":303434,"title":"","content":"He earns a free icecream and happy meal at McDonalds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T12:03:32-08:00","id":303568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/301846-what-happens-when-a-wraith-resolves-a-fetter?p=303434#post303434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He earns a free icecream and happy meal at McDonalds</div> </div> </div> </div>And the ability to actually consume it and take pleasure from it, which is why it's so impressive for a Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T12:09:25-08:00","id":303579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/301846-what-happens-when-a-wraith-resolves-a-fetter?p=303434#post303434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He earns a free icecream and happy meal at McDonalds</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/301846-what-happens-when-a-wraith-resolves-a-fetter?p=303568#post303568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the ability to actually consume it and take pleasure from it, which is why it's so impressive for a Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will the toy become a new fetter or a relic?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T12:19:31-08:00","id":303589,"title":"","content":"Plastic can't be a Relic (personal opinion, not canon).<br /> <br /> But this Fetter can travel in the Wraith's pocket, which has many benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 11-05-2014, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T13:23:47-08:00","id":303692,"title":"","content":"i think it would be more funny if the wraith just got the happy meal, no toys and no ability to consume it, just to have it there xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:00:42-08:00","id":304128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/301846-what-happens-when-a-wraith-resolves-a-fetter?p=303321#post303321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more reaching an emotional state in which you can let something go. You still care about it, but you're no longer hung up on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The relevant quote from Wraith 2e, p. 231: &amp;quot;There are those rare wraiths who Resolved all of their Fetters, to whom rumor grants the ability to travel anywhere in the Underworld.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I.E., their existence is a known thing, what they can do is a rumour.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks everyone, I appreciate the info. I was never that in to Wraith, so it's good to hear this from knowledgable sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",